cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite the archived release and the accompanying manuscript."
title: "lvi-measurement-validity: measurement-validity assessment for tightly coupled LiDAR-visual-inertial odometry"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "H0risans"
version: "0.3.2-w4c"
date-released: "2026-11-21"
license: "MIT"
repository-code: "https://github.com/H0risans/lvi-measurement-validity"
url: "https://github.com/H0risans/lvi-measurement-validity"
abstract: >-
  Research code and derived data for event-level fault injection, processing-exposure
  verification, measurement-validity assessment, and output-hold supervision in
  tightly coupled LiDAR-visual-inertial odometry. The release accompanies the
  manuscript "When Is a Visual Measurement Still Valid? Event-Level Injection and
  Output Hold in Tightly Coupled LiDAR-Visual-Inertial Odometry".
keywords:
  - measurement validity
  - fault injection
  - measurement traceability
  - LiDAR-visual-inertial odometry
  - pose error
  - output hold
